#N canvas 40 40 640 460 12;
#X text 20 10 ATOM SQ synth: the pads are a piano keyboard (bottom row white keys \, top row black keys \, octave + / - to move) playing the piano voices. PLAY = autoplay Clair de Lune \, PLAY again = pause / resume \, STOP = stop and back to the start. knobs and screen buttons depend on the page (atom-sq-pages): PLAY \, INSTRUMENT \, PRACTICE (LEFT / RIGHT / BOTH hands) \, MUSIC. set MIDI to the SQ and the audio output in Media > Audio Settings. DSP comes on by itself;
#X obj 420 60 atom-sq-map;
#X obj 20 60 r sq-key;
#X obj 20 90 unpack f f;
#X obj 20 120 poly 16 1;
#X obj 20 150 pack f f f;
#X obj 20 180 clone -s 1 piano-voice 16;
#X obj 20 220 lop~ 12000;
#X obj 20 260 *~;
#X obj 20 300 dac~;
#X obj 120 220 eq3;
#X text 1100 560 instruments: 0 E.PIANO (piano-voice) \, the only one for now. sq-do-inst N releases held notes and stores the choice in sqinst. grand-voice.pd (a synthesized piano) is kept but not loaded: its attack sounded wrong;
#X obj 1100 620 r sq-do-inst;
#X obj 1100 680 t f b;
#X msg 1200 710 stop;
#X obj 1100 740 v sqinst;
#X obj 1300 620 loadbang;
#X msg 1300 650 0;
